  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1204.15 Rotogravure printing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1204.15 \"Rotogravure printing\" means the application of ink in the form of characters, designs, or pictures to a substrate by means of a roll printing technique in which the image area is recessed relative to the non-image area.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
